# STATUS: DEPOSITED 2026-06-12 on Zenodo as version "1.0". Concept (cite-all) DOI
# 10.5281/zenodo.20663484; version DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20663485. The top-level doi: is
# the concept DOI (cite-all), with both DOIs listed under identifiers:, mirroring the
# pcf-delta convention. All four reference DOIs below were verified live via doi.org 302
# redirect to zenodo.org on 2026-06-10 (not asserted from memory). License: code is
# Apache-2.0 (Lean formalization + sympy harness); the repo also ships the documenting
# manuscript higher_casoratian.tex/.pdf (entry C1) under the same Apache-2.0 (no separate
# CC-BY-4.0 was applied to the PDF at deposit). Public GitHub
# repo https://github.com/papanokechi/pcf-casoratian-catalogue. Future revisions deposit
# via Zenodo "New version" under the concept DOI; operator-gated -- do NOT cut a new
# version without operator sign-off.
# VERSION 1.1 (deposited 2026-08-02, version DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21753829, from git tag
# v1.1): promotes the Section-7
# fundamental-system converse (STRUCTURAL -> PROVEN: sol_unique_of_init,
# solution_isLinearCombo) and adds a now-PROVEN Hermite-Pade/Apery irrationality pipeline
# (namespace PcfHermitePade, source HermitePade.lean) re-deriving Irrational phi via the
# order-3 Casoratian (goldenRatio_irrational_via_caso); the formalized core grows from
# nine to twenty-six declarations (all cones subset of {propext, Classical.choice,
# Quot.sound}, captured live 2026-06-13; full corpus 86 cones). A peer-review hardening pass
# added the bridge lemma caso3_matches_general (bespoke caso3 = det casoMat at k=2) and
# corrected the manuscript notation (matrix W vs determinant C=det W), the sqrt5 honesty
# wording, and the linear-form criterion naming. No novelty is claimed for phi's irrationality
# (classical; Mathlib's is sqrt5-based) -- only for the converse and the reusable pipeline.
# date-released and version above are provisional; a v1.1 version DOI will exist only after
# the operator commits and mints a Zenodo "New version" under concept DOI
# 10.5281/zenodo.20663484. The v1.0 version DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20663485 is unchanged.
